<title>QATAR: Qatar Islamic Bank lifts 1996 profits.</title>
<headline>Qatar Islamic Bank lifts 1996 profits.</headline>
<dateline>DOHA 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>			  (million Qatari riyals, rounded)</p>
<p>					1996		1995</p>
<p>Net Profit			  35.1		12.1</p>
<p>Total income		    203.47	     172.37</p>
<p>Total expenses		   90.99		71.98</p>
<p>Depositors' share in income  83.59		87.44</p>
<p>Provision			  15.00		32.00</p>
<p>Cash dividend		     9.00		 9.00</p>
<p>Total assets (billion)	  3.03		 2.83</p>
<p>Shareholders funds	    217.53	     186.55</p>
<p>Full name: Qatar Islamic Bank (S.A.Q.)</p>
<p>NOTE: The bank maintained its dividend at six percent of capital. It said it could not distribute more to shareholders because it provide for bad investments in the collapsed Bank of Credit and Commerce International (BCCI) despite higher profits.</p>
</text>
